   {
    "name": "insurance.txt",
    "text": "CERT OF INS.   REF EV-23327\nMeridian Mutual Insurance   POL NO EL-169198\nINSURED ....... Halden Valley Harriers\nRISK LOCATION .. Westbrook\nFROM .......... 16 October 2027\nTO ............ 18 October 2027\nINDEMNITY ..... $2,000,000\nACTIVITY ...... Foot race (Valley Harriers Spring Dash 10K)\nISSUED ........ 14 September 2027\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "medical_plan.txt",
    "text": "Valley Harriers Spring Dash 10K - medical notes\nSunday 17 October 2027 / gun 08:30 / 180 runners / 10K\ncontact Anita Bose 555-0141\nNo ambulance will be stationed at the race; any ambulance would come through the 911 system.\n\nFIRST AID\ncommittee members w/ work first aid certs. kit at HQ tent + kit in lead car\n\nWEATHER / WATER\nwater every 2.5k. forecast check -48h and -2h. >28C earlier start or shorter course. >32C cancel. foil + warm tent at finish if cold/wet\n\nHOSPITAL\nHarbourside Medical Centre, 6km from finish. pickup point the bandstand, route walked w/ first aiders. ED told date + numbers\n\nCOMMS\nradios on medical channel at all posts + bikes, phones backup. amb calls go via medical lead, who gives crew the barrier to come to\n\nLEAD\nrace director + committee\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "race_plan.txt",
    "text": "RACE PLAN\nValley Harriers Spring Dash 10K | Sunday 17 October 2027\nOrganiser: Halden Valley Harriers\nRace director: Anita Bose\nReference: RQ-96122\n\nOverview\nThe Valley Harriers Spring Dash 10K is a 10K race of 10 km for 180 entrants, based in the Westbrook area of Port Halden. The start is at 08:30 and the course closes at 10:30.\n\nCourse\nThe course stays entirely on the Ferry Park ring path and the Old Mill Trail, away from the highway, and no road is closed for the race. The finish is at the old mill car park.\n\nCourse dimensions\nUsable width on the Ferry Park ring path is 2.5 m and on the Old Mill Trail 2 m, with water or fencing on both sides for almost the whole distance. There are no run-offs apart from the finish area, which measures roughly 15 m by 10 m.\n\nSupport\nEntrants collect numbers from the bandstand from one hour before the start. Timing is by chip, with mats at the start and finish. Results are posted on the Valley Harriers website the same day.\n"
   }
  ],
  "cover_letter": "14 September 2027\n\nEvents Office\nCity of Port Halden\n\nDear Events Officer,\n\nI am writing on behalf of our organisation about this year's race.\n\nWe are applying for a street race permit for the Valley Harriers Spring Dash 10K on Sunday 17 October 2027. We expect 180 runners over 10K, starting at 08:30 in the Westbrook area. The completed form and the attachments (insurance.txt, medical_plan.txt, race_plan.txt) are enclosed.\n\nPlease let me know if you need anything else.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nAnita Bose\nVolunteer Coordinator, Halden Valley Harriers\nanita@valleyharriers.example / 555-0141\n",
